# feat: [PROTOTYPE - DO NOT MERGE] catalog pricing state for price-on-request variants
#
# Conventional-commit message for the candidate patch below (header only;
# nothing was committed). Responds to Universal-Commerce-Protocol/ucp#877.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-10-05 (second maintainer-feedback pass) to reflect the
# RESOLVED `contract_only` position. This revision REVERSES part of the
# immediately prior patch revision (same date, first pass):
#   - `contract_only` is restored to the "forbid price" rule alongside
#     `quote_required` (rule 1's `if` condition is `enum: ["quote_required",
#     "contract_only"]` again, not `const: "quote_required"`). A resolved/
#     entitled response now transitions to `buyer_specific` + `price` instead
#     of retaining `contract_only` with a price — `contract_only` + a numeric
#     `price` is INVALID again, matching the schema's state before the first
#     pass's relaxation.
#   - `pricing.mode` remains an OPEN VOCABULARY (unaffected by the reversal
#     above — this part of the first pass is preserved, not re-litigated).
#     Well-known values stay in `examples`; an unrecognized mode still does
#     not fail validation on its own.
#   - `next_step` is documented more precisely as orthogonal to `price`: its
#     presence never implies `price` must be absent, and it does not
#     participate in the conditional `price` rules (no schema change beyond
#     prose — `next_step` was never referenced by any `allOf` branch).
#   - `price_range`/`list_price_range` prose is refined from "carries a
#     numeric price" to "range-eligible price," since an unknown `mode` may
#     legally coexist with a numeric `price` for forward compatibility while
#     remaining unsafe for an unaware Platform to fold into a range (prose
#     only; no schema-logic change to the `allOf` structure in product.json).
#
# See research/price-on-request/DESIGN.md §2B/§2C/§2D, COMPATIBILITY.md, and
# EP_SUBMISSION_DRAFT.md for full detail on this reversal and the newly
# documented (but NOT schema-implemented) Purchase Options (#901) composition
# analysis.
#
# ---- First-pass changes (2026-10-05, earlier the same date; mostly
# superseded by the reversal above, kept for history) ----
#   - `pricing.mode` was made an OPEN VOCABULARY (the closed `enum` was
#     removed; well-known values moved to `examples`).
#   - `contract_only` no longer forbade `price` (relaxed, not resolved): the
#     "forbid price" allOf rule was scoped to `quote_required` only. REVERSED
#     by this regeneration — see above.
#   - Priced `buyer_specific` responses (mode retained alongside `price`)
#     were documented as the PROPOSED NORMATIVE behavior — UNCHANGED by this
#     regeneration, still in effect.
#   - Cache-isolation requirements for buyer-specific prices — and values
#     derived from them, explicitly including a product's `price_range` —
#     were stated in prose as explicit MUST-level normative language —
#     UNCHANGED by this regeneration, still in effect, now with an added NDA
#     nuance (buyer_specific does not imply per-person-computed uniqueness).
#
# NOTE (corrected 2026-10-02, reconfirmed 2026-10-05 twice): the `feat:`
# prefix is PROVISIONAL, not final. Release classification (minor vs major)
# is an open EP/TC decision pending the project's versioning ruling. The
# compatibility analysis (COMPATIBILITY.md) shows this is NOT purely additive:
# baseline-valid payloads carrying a `pricing` field (permitted via
# additionalProperties) change validity under the proposal -- (a) price +
# mode `quote_required` OR `contract_only` goes valid -> invalid (conflict
# rejection, restored to cover BOTH known modes as of this regeneration);
# (b) malformed `pricing` shapes (null, `{}`, non-object mode carrier) go
# valid -> invalid. Unknown `pricing.mode` values still do not narrow (open
# vocabulary, unaffected by the `contract_only` reversal) -- this remains a
# reduction versus the ORIGINAL closed-enum version of this patch, but the
# change is NOT purely additive: two narrowing classes remain (conflict
# rejection across two known modes, and malformed-pricing-shape rejection).
# The differential fuzz (Leg E) plus the pricing-mode fuzz leg (Leg G,
# updated this regeneration so `contract_only` expects `price` to be absent)
# establishes no-regression ONLY for the generated priced subset; it does
# not imply universal compatibility.
#
# PROPOSED - requires a TC-approved Enhancement Proposal before any
# implementation PR (per org CONTRIBUTING.md). This prototype implies no
# agreement from maintainers or the Technical Council.
#
# Base: Universal-Commerce-Protocol/ucp @ b0e81adecf816a1771b736464f17586d76950f7f
# Files: 2 files changed (source/schemas/shopping/types/{variant,product}.json)
# Diff below is schema-only (variant.json + product.json), per the
# second-pass regeneration instructions; the doc-prose patch (catalog/index.md,
# catalog/search.md) and the price_filter.json/warning_code.json prose
# patches from the original prototype publication are unaffected by this
# round's schema reversal and are not repeated here.

